# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings. These files are executed by bash on
# Linux — over SSH, in WSL, on the GPU box — and a CR at the end of every
# line makes bash fail with `$'\r': command not found` on line 1, which reads
# like a corrupt script rather than a line-ending problem.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and rewrote deploy.sh to CRLF
# on checkout, which is exactly how that happened.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
